  subgraph G_D1["D1 - Market, shadow price, spread"]
    M["ERCOT day-ahead, nodal"] --> P1["Nodal price<br/>LMP_i = λ + Σ_k SF_k,i · μ_k"]
    P1 --> P2["Energy component λ<br/>same at every node"]
    P1 --> P3["Congestion component<br/>Σ_k SF · μ, location-specific"]
    P3 --> SP["Shadow price μ_k<br/>μ_k = marginal cost of relaxing<br/>constraint k by 1 MW"]
    SP --> EX_D1["Example: road at capacity<br/>one more MW costs +$20<br/>therefore μ = $20/MWh"]
    SP --> TOPK["Selection: per hour, per constraint<br/>sort by its own μ descending, take top 50<br/>binding only, snapshot lagged 24 h (previous day's clearing)"]
    P1 --> SPREAD["Path spread<br/>ΔLMP_s→d = LMP_d - LMP_s<br/>= Σ_k (SF_k,d - SF_k,s) · μ_k<br/>= Σ_k ΔSF_k · μ_k"]
    SPREAD --> C1["λ cancels exactly<br/>spread = pure congestion differential"]
    SPREAD --> DSF_D1["Differential shift factor<br/>ΔSF_k = SF_k,d - SF_k,s<br/>Example: 0.6 - 0.1 = 0.5<br/>If μ_k = $20/MWh, contribution = $10/MWh"]
    DSF_D1 --> Z["If ΔSF_k = 0, the constraint affects both ends equally<br/>Contribution to the spread = 0"]
    SP --> ARG["WHY THIS IS THE RIGHT ASSUMPTION<br/>μ is the market's own signal of<br/>where and how badly the grid is constrained"]
    ARG --> DOM["Needs domain understanding,<br/>not just sending prices to ML. And that is shown by our results"]
    ARG --> LINK["Outcome link (canonical raw, 5-seed)<br/>price-only models: good center, bad risk<br/>LQR coverage 73.1%, crosses 32.0%<br/>SPARC 89.4%, crosses 0.1%"]
  end

  subgraph G_D2["D2 - SCED, the anchor, our move"]
    SCED["SCED optimization<br/>solved every hour"] --> OUT["Outputs simultaneously<br/>LMPs, binding constraints, shadow prices"]
    OUT --> IDENTITY["LMP identity is EXACT at the optimum<br/>LMP_i = λ + Σ_k SF_k,i · μ_k<br/>λ, SF, μ are the primal and dual<br/>quantities of the optimization"]
    IDENTITY --> ENDOG["But they are ENDOGENOUS<br/>defined only by solving the clearing<br/>no closed-form function from raw inputs"]
    ENDOG --> RESOLVE["Computing them means re-solving SCED<br/>a large complementarity problem,<br/>not a differentiable layer"]
    OUT --> DSF_D2["ΔSF is not published for each<br/>source-destination pair<br/>depends on topology + operating point"]
    RESOLVE --> MUST["Rule is real, but NOT transcribable<br/>so LEARN the exposure weights"]
    DSF_D2 --> MUST

    ANCHOR["Anchor: Yu et al., Austria<br/>MRINN"] --> RULE["Known piecewise settlement formula<br/>embedded as differentiable layers<br/>= RULE-EMBEDDING"]
    RULE --> HARD["Hard hierarchical head<br/>non-crossing by construction, AQCR = 0"]
    RULE --> GAPS["Never reports coverage, Winkler, CRPS, PIT"]

    MUST --> MOVE["Our move: condition on the PAST published clearing outputs<br/>previous day's clearing (t-24 h, ADR-0013) - the freshest snapshot available at bid time<br/>the target hour's own μ is NOT used —<br/>it exists only after that hour clears, so using it would leak"]
    MOVE --> LEARN["What is given: the lagged μ (a published output)<br/>What is learned: ΔSF, as attention weights"]
    MOVE --> NOT["SPARC is constraint-aware<br/>NOT market-rule-informed"]
    MOVE --> WHICH["Which rule do we embed? NONE<br/>the identity is used as structure"]
    MOVE --> QRESOLVE["Q: couldn't you differentiate through SCED?<br/>In principle yes, but it needs a full, maintainable<br/>ERCOT SCED model with complementarity — a different,<br/>much larger program. The clearing outputs are already published."]
  end

  subgraph G_D3["D3 - The model"]
    IN["Inputs<br/>top-50 constraint slots (μ, identity, kV, flow)<br/>temporal Fourier, 3 lagged spreads, path embedding"] --> ID
    IN --> MU
    ID["Identity pathway<br/>MEAN-POOLED over binding constraints<br/>fixed size because K varies hourly<br/>captures WHICH set of corridors binds"] --> ATTN_D3
    MU["Shadow-price pathway<br/>per-slot keys and values<br/>the VALUES carry the shadow-price (μ) signal"] --> ATTN_D3
    TEMP["Temporal encoder"] --> ATTN_D3
    Q["Query = the path asking<br/>which constraints matter for me"] --> ATTN_D3
    ATTN_D3["Constraint attention<br/>a_k = exp(score_k) / Σ_j exp(score_j)<br/>Σ_k a_k = 1<br/>a_k = learned relative exposure weight<br/>(plays the role of ΔSF: positive + normalized,<br/>so it captures relative magnitude; sign and scale<br/>are absorbed downstream)"] --> HEAD
    ATTN_D3 --> BLEND["Weighted blend of the value signals<br/>≈ Σ_k a_k · μ_k<br/>same form as Σ_k ΔSF_k · μ_k"]
    HEAD["Quantile head<br/>soft flat head + crossing penalty<br/>raw AQCR 0.11% vs LQR 32.0%, MLP 15.1%<br/>(soft head; hard head 0.00% by construction)"] --> LOSS["Training loss<br/>L = Σ_t Σ_τ ρ_τ(y_t - q_hat_τ,t) + λ · crossing penalty<br/>ρ_τ(u) = u · (τ - I[u &lt; 0])<br/>penalty is training-only, never a metric"]
    HEAD --> HARD2["Hard (hierarchical) head tested on SPARC<br/>calibrated Winkler 18.00 (hard) vs 18.20 (soft) → comparable; kept soft as flagship"]
    LAG["Lagged-spread encoder"] --> HEAD

    ATTN_D3 --> WHY_ROOT["Why attention, not something else?"]
    WHY_ROOT --> A1["Raw concatenation of the constraints<br/>REJECTED<br/>the number of binding constraints changes every hour<br/>the network needs a fixed-size input"]
    WHY_ROOT --> A2["Mean-pool everything<br/>REJECTED<br/>treats every binding line as equally important for every path<br/>destroys selectivity: a line near the sink should matter more than one far away"]
    WHY_ROOT --> A3["MLP over the constraint features<br/>REJECTED<br/>no explicit weight per constraint<br/>cannot tell you which line drove the forecast"]
    WHY_ROOT --> A4["RNN or Transformer over the constraint set<br/>REJECTED<br/>a set has no order; first and last are interchangeable<br/>imposes an order that does not exist"]
    WHY_ROOT --> WIN["ATTENTION — CHOSEN<br/>handles a variable-size set<br/>gives a per-path weight to each constraint<br/>order-free (permutation-invariant)<br/>the weights play the role of learned ΔSF<br/>→ interpretable by construction"]
    WHYID["Why mean pooling (identity pathway)<br/>K varies each hour → need a fixed-size vector<br/>order-independent and robust<br/>captures WHICH set of corridors binds"]
    OTHERS["What others do, and why it is wrong for this problem<br/>feed the price as a time series, never see the constraint set<br/>= model the shadow, not the cause"]
    WHYID --> OTHERS
  end

  subgraph G_D4["D4 - Metrics"]
    EX_D4["Running example<br/>Observed value: y = 10<br/>90% interval: [L, U] = [-5, 15]<br/>Median forecast: q_0.5 = 8"] --> AQL
    EX_D4 --> COV
    EX_D4 --> WINK
    EX_D4 --> AQCR
    AQL["AQL / pinball loss<br/>ρ_τ(y - q_τ) = (y - q_τ) · (τ - I[y &lt; q_τ])<br/>At τ = 0.5: error 2 → loss 1.0<br/>At τ = 0.9: error 2 → loss 1.8<br/>standard quantile loss; the anchor's headline"]
    COV["Empirical interval coverage<br/>Coverage = (1/N) · Σ_t I[L_t ≤ y_t ≤ U_t]<br/>For a 90% interval: L_t = q_0.1 and U_t = q_0.9<br/>88 of 100 hours inside = 88%<br/>THE decision metric: a desk sizes from the band"]
    WINK["Winkler score for a 90% interval<br/>W = U - L, if L ≤ y ≤ U<br/>W = U - L + 20(L - y), if y &lt; L<br/>W = U - L + 20(y - U), if y &gt; U<br/>rewards covering AND narrow; cannot be gamed with a wide box"]
    AQCR["Adjacent quantile crossing rate<br/>AQCR = crossings / adjacent quantile pairs<br/>A crossing occurs when q_τ,j &gt; q_τ,j+1<br/>SPARC 0.11% vs LQR 31.99%"]
    CRPS["CRPS<br/>proper score on the whole predictive CDF<br/>rewards calibration + sharpness"]
    PIT["PIT / KS<br/>actual 10, forecast CDF 0.5 → PIT 0.5<br/>uniform = calibrated; U-shape = too narrow; cap = too wide<br/>EVERY method fails uniformity → comparative claim only"]
    EFF["Efficiency<br/>8,978 params vs MLP 64,456 / Transformer 78,536<br/>enables frequent retraining"]
    SIG["Significance<br/>5 seeds → paired t / Wilcoxon / sign<br/>coverage vs LQR: t = 8.33, p = 0.0011"]
    QUANT["Concrete quantile example<br/>point: spread = 8 dollars, hides the risk<br/>quantiles: median 8, 90% band [-5, 15]<br/>if spread realizes 30, the point forecast was useless<br/>0.90 tells you the worst plausible case<br/>weather analogy: 25C vs 18-27C with 90% chance<br/>0.10 and 0.90 = the band a desk sizes from"]
    AQL --> PARADOX["THE METRIC-PARADOX<br/>AQL is middle-dominated → LQR wins it<br/>Winkler taxes the band edges → SPARC wins it<br/>the reported winner is an artifact of the metric"]
    COV --> TRADE["Why calibration matters for trading<br/>a band claiming 90% but holding 73%<br/>leaves 27% of hours under-hedged<br/>losses live in the missed hours, not the mean error<br/>low mean error does NOT rescue bad intervals"]
    PARADOX --> TRADE
    WINK --> TAILNOTE["No tail contradiction<br/>Winkler tails = the 0.10 and 0.90 edges of the NORMAL band<br/>spike hours = top 5% EXTREME events, far beyond 0.90<br/>different things; extreme events are OUT OF SCOPE here"]
  end

  subgraph G_D5["D5 - Protocol, findings, mechanism (canonical 5-seed)"]
    PROTO["Protocol<br/>CPU, chronological 70-15-15<br/>5 seeds 42-46, 7 quantiles<br/>AQL = pure pinball; penalty training-only"] --> WHY5["Why 5 seeds<br/>one run can be lucky<br/>5 seeds give mean ± std and paired tests<br/>a single-seed win is never a claim"]
